  "sport": "basketball",
  "title": "Round the cones – 1v1 back to the basket",
  "description": "Put two cones (or chairs) side by side on the right half of the court, just short of the half-court line. Two players start on the baseline opposite the cones, and the one nearer the sideline has the ball. On the signal both go at full speed – one dribbling, one sprinting – round their own cone on the right side and turn back towards the basket. After the turn it is live 1v1: the ball handler attacks, the other player defends. The next pair is ready on the baseline and goes as soon as the play is over; switch roles every time.\n\nProgression: allow only two dribbles after the turn, so the attacker has to decide quickly and go straight at the rim.\n\nFull-court variant: place one pair of cones just above the free-throw line extended and another pair past half-court. The players cross at both pairs – the dribbler takes the inside cone and the runner the outside one at the first pair, then the other way round – and play 1v1 at the far basket. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Full speed from the start – the turn round the cone should be tight and quick."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Attacker: keep your eyes up through the turn and attack before the defender is set."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Defender: sprint back on the shortest line and get between the ball and the basket."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Finish at speed – lay-up or pull-up, then crash for the rebound."
    }
  ],
